From 1a8687ad8e526f12775778b2e25fa1dfaf0e593e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:39:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/31] android, ipa: simple: Support touch to focus

Android sends an AF region and an AF trigger when the user touches the
preview, but only to a camera that reports AF modes, one AF region and
a non-zero minimum focus distance. The HAL reported AF off and a fixed
focus lens, so the autofocus ran inside the IPA and ignored touches.

- The software ISP takes the autofocus contrast window from the
  parameters, as fractions of the processed window.
- The simple IPA autofocus handles AfMode, AfMetering, AfWindows and
  AfTrigger when the lens has a focus control: a trigger scans the
  whole range in the new window and holds the result until a cancel,
  and a new window alone rescans in continuous mode. It reports
  AfState.
- The HAL reports the AF modes, one AF region and a minimum focus
  distance, translates the AF mode, region and trigger, and runs
  Android's AF state machine over the AfState reported by the IPA.

Assisted-by: LLM
